Home menu: ORIGINAL 4:3, the PS1's own picture with black bars at the sides.

Reported: there was no original PS1 aspect option - 4:3 with black bars left
and right. The renderer could pillarbox all along, but only when four
settings agreed: aspect 4:3, Image fit Letterbox, no zoom or stretch, and no
overscan crop (trimming the blank lines makes the kept band wider than 4:3,
gpu_gl_renderer.c overscan_aspect_mul). Picking 4:3 reset none of them, so a
4:3 left on Stretch, or on the Enhanced preset's stretch 100 and 12/12 crop,
filled a 16:9 window.

psx_pause_menu.c/.h: psx_pause_menu_set_aspect_original(). Aspect index 0
reads ORIGINAL 4:3 while the framing is the original's, with the note "THE
PS1'S OWN SHAPE, WITH BLACK BARS AT THE SIDES. APPLIES WHEN YOU RESUME."; a 4:3
the launcher zoomed or stretched reads plain 4:3.

main.cpp:
- picking index 0 also applies the original framing at once
  (pause_menu_apply_original_framing): letterbox, which clears zoom and
  stretch, no pan, no overscan crop. Presentation only, so safe from the pause
  loop; the aspect is staged as before;
- g_overscan_crop mirrors the crop handed to the renderer (PSX_OVERSCAN_CROP,
  clamped the same way), so pause_menu_framing_is_original() can tell - the
  same test as the launcher's config.is_original_43;
- MENU_PREF_OVERSCAN: menu_prefs_write emits overscan_top/bottom/left/right,
  which launcher/crash2launcher/ingame.py folds back as one change, "game
  aspect original 4:3".

Any Home-menu aspect change still drops native-wide to the squash mode, as
before (pause_menu_flush_pending).

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake.

